## What a `guidance` memory is

**Guidance is an abstract supertype** — the category of memorials that prescribe action.  They tell future sessions *how to behave*: do-this-because, don't-do-this-because, reach-for-this, be-this-way.  Concrete subtypes carry positive conventions (`pattern`), negative conventions (`anti-pattern`), meta-rules governing the memory system (`protocol`), aesthetic / style filters (`preference`), corrections from the human collaborator (`feedback`), and explicit collaboration rules (`interaction`).

Contrast with the sibling abstract supertypes:

- **`signal`** — captures observation ("here is what we noticed")
- **`artifact`** — produces durable output (decision / plan / library study)
- **`meta`** — schema / structural ("about the map, not the territory")

## When `extends: guidance` helps

Category-level rules become expressible across the family:

- *"Every guidance should cite at least one signal that motivated it"* — normative rules need empirical grounding (observed need produces rule)
- *"Every guidance must carry claim-shaped `name:` (title-as-API)"* — Zettelkasten-derived discipline; the title states the rule
- *"Every anti-pattern must `contradict` at least one positive guidance"* — every negative carries its positive alternative
- *"Guidance with `at-startup: keystone` is surfaced TIER-0 at session start"* — the discipline-visibility surface

Without supertype membership, each rule enumerates the concrete subtypes manually.  With it, `is-a? guidance` becomes the predicate, and the rule survives the addition of new subtypes.

## At-startup visibility tier

Guidance memorials can opt into the at-startup-visibility surface via the `at-startup:` frontmatter field:

- **`keystone`** — disciplines whose violation is the most-frequently-observed failure mode; surfaced TIER-0 at the SessionStart hook + project-root CLAUDE.md
- **`high`** — high-frequency, broad-applicability guidance; surfaced TIER-1
- **`standard`** (default) — surfaced on-demand only (reachable via `/memory-search` and `/memory-ground`, not auto-loaded)

A paired `one-line:` field carries the hand-curated short label rendered in the at-startup banner.  Required when `at-startup:` is set.  Kept under ~80 chars for one-line-per-entry rendering.

The cache regenerator walks all guidance memorials, filters by presence of `at-startup:`, and emits a sorted-vector EDN keyed by rel-path.  Tier calibration is reviewed at retrospective time; thresholds (e.g., `keystone` ≤7, `high` ≤15) are soft ceilings.

## Not instantiated directly

Don't write a memorial with `type: guidance` — write one of the concrete subtypes (e.g., `type: pattern`, `type: anti-pattern`, `type: protocol`, `type: preference`, `type: feedback`, `type: interaction`), each of which declares this class as its parent via `:dt/subclass-of`.  The `abstract?: true` schema flag marks this class as non-instantiable.

